Version 2.7 DRAFT

	  Student, Faculty, and Staff Computer Usage Policy
	      for the use of Computer Services Resources
		     of Mankato State University

                      
*Definitions:
------------------------------
Administration: Current administration as defined by the appropriate
	state contracts.

CWIS : Campus-Wide Information System

Faculty : Current faculty, current adjunct faculty, and approved
	emerti faculty as defined by the appropriate state contracts.

Group Account : A Userid which is established for a group of Users.

MSUCS : Mankato State University Department of Computer Services.

MSU : Mankato State University.

Personal Use : Those activities which are not directly related to the
	educational, professional, instructional, administrative, or
	outreach activities of a user's role with MSU.

Resource : Any inanimate piece of equipment or property of that
	equipment which is controlled and administered by MSUCS,
	including but not limited to computers, telecommunications
	lines, computer memory, printers, printer paper,
	computer disk space, and networks.

Resource-Specific Policy : A policy that:
	1. falls under the jurisdiction of this policy
		and
	2. applies only to a specific resource.

Staff : Current staff and approved emerti staff as defined by the
	appropriate state contracts.

Student : Individuals who are enrolled for at least 1 credit during
	the current academic term.

User : A person who is authorized to use a resource controlled by
	MSUCS.

Userid : A unique label referring to a specific authorized user,
	commonly used by computer system software to track individual
	users.

Visitor : Those people who:
		1) are not students, faculty, staff, or administration
		2) do not have a legally binding contract with MSU
		3) have been given authorization by MSUCS to use
			specific MSUCS resources for a specific
			purpose.



*Scope of Policy
----------------------------------------------------------------------
This policy applies to all persons who have been authorized to use
MSUCS resources.


Relationship of this policy to all other policies:
----------------------------------------------------------------------
This policy is not intended to replace in part or in whole, the MSU
Statement of Student Responsibilities, MSU faculty or staff employment
contracts, federal law, state law, local law, or any other legally
binding document.  This policy exists in addition to all other legally
binding documents to guide the conduct of Users and MSUCS in regards
to MSUCS resources.

Some resources will have policies of their own regarding their use.
These policies are referred to as "Resource Specific Policies".  The
Resource Specific Policies do not replace this policy, they simply
specify any additional conditions of use that users must respect when
using that resource.

This policy may be superseded, on an individual basis, by a legally
binding contract.  If this is the case, then all parties involved will
be notified of this fact before the individuals are granted
authorization.


*Spirit of the Policy
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Educational computing resources under the control of MSUCS are for the
use by the students, faculty, and staff of MSU in the instructional,
academic, research, educational, administrative, professional and
outreach activities of MSU.

Users are individually accountable for their own behavior with MSUCS
resources.  Using MSUCS resources does not exempt the user from any
other laws or obligations.  Any actions which intentionally try to
circumvent the accountability of a user, maliciously interfere with
other user's use of resources, or engage in fraudulent activities is
prohibited.

It is intended that all parties to this policy will act in a spirit of
cooperation, and in a mature, responsible, respectful, efficient,
ethical and legal manner.



*Obtaining Authorization
----------------------------------------------------------------------
All students, faculty, and staff are considered to be candidates for
authorized usage.

To become an authorized user of a resource, users must fill out the
appropriate forms to request authorization from MSUCS or make an
appointment with the administrator of the resource.

All Visitors must obtain authorization directly from the Director of
Academic Computing Systems in Computer Services.



*Due Process
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Violations of this policy will be either handled directly by MSUCS or
the violation will be submitted to the Judicial Affairs Coordinator.

If the violation is to be handled by MSUCS, then MSUCS will follow the
minimum due process rights as outlined in the Statement of Student
Responsibilities.

Visitors will fall under this policy as if they were students.
However, any violations by visitors will be handled by MSUCS, not the
Judicial Affairs Coordinator.


*Consequences of violating this policy.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
If the user has been referred to the Judicial Board, then this section
will not apply.

If MSUCS decides to handle a violation, then the consequences of
violating this policy include, but are not limited to: verbal
warnings, removal of authorization from some or all MSUCS resources,
and/or restrictions on user access to some or all MSUCS resources.

The exact consequence(s), if any, will vary depending upon the
specific violation.

The consequences will be enforced regardless of educational, research,
instructional, or any other obligations, including class assignments,
which may require the user to have access to the resources in
question.

The consequences will be honored across those times in which the user
is not associated with MSU or MSUCS.



*Disclaimers
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  MSUCS cannot accept responsibility for any form of loss of data
due to a users use, MSUCS's use, random events, nor any consequential
loss or damage.

2.  MSUCS cannot be held responsible for failed equipment, including
backups.

3.  MSUCS provides no guarantee of any particular kind of services for
any user on any resource.

4.  MSUCS provides no guarantee of the accuracy or continued accuracy
of any resource under MSUCS control.  This includes stored data,
communications, computations, programs, and communicated messages.

5.  MSUCS provides no guarantee of absolute privacy.  There is an
acknowledged trade-off between the absolute right of privacy of a
user, and the need of MSUCS to gather necessary information to ensure
the continued functioning of MSUCS controlled resources.

6.  The availability of material or information on any service
provided by MSUCS or the ability to obtain material or information by
using MSUCS resources, does not imply that MSUCS or MSU approves,
verifies the accuracy of, or endorses its content.


*Rights and Responsibilities of Users
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1.0  Security

1.1 Users have the responsibility to use secure passwords for the
	resources which they are authorized to use.

		Refer to the password creation procedure for more information
	on choosing a secure password.

	1.2 Users have the responsibility to keep all passwords secret at all
	times.

	Users should NEVER tell any other person their password for
	any MSUCS resource.

	Users will NEVER need to tell their passwords to any MSU
	employee; authorized MSUCS employee's will have the
	appropriate privileges on the resources in question and will
	not need your password to gain access to your account.

	
1.3 Users have the responsibility to utilize security mechanisms
	provided by the resource(s) to keep their own files, data, and
	communications from other users.

	If users disable the security mechanisms that are provided,
	they should be aware that they are still responsible for any
	violation of this policy that occurs involving their account
	or access privileges.

	
1.4 Users have the responsibility to identify themselves in any
	communication which uses MSUCS resources.

	Users have the responsibility to provide valid, traceable
	identification if requested by computer applications or servers
	controlled by MSUCS or in establishing connections from MSUCS
	resources.

	
2.0  Authorization.

2.1  Users can not authorize other people to use any resources which
	fall under this policy.

	This includes, but is not limited to: "sharing" passwords or
	userids, use of any kind of trusted-host facilities,
	anonymous use of resources, or disabling security mechanisms
	to allow any non-authorized persons access to MSUCS resources.

	2.2 Users have the responsibility to use only those resources to which
	they have been given authorization to use.

	2.3 Users the have responsibility to access resources by using only
	those userids or methods that they have been authorized to
	use.

	
3.0 Policy

3.1 Users have the responsibility to abide by any law or legally
	binding documents, including but not limited to: federal law,
	state law, or the Statement of Student Responsibilities; while
	using MSUCS resources.

		
3.2 Users have the responsibility to read, understand and comply with
	the most current version of this policy and any
	resource-specific policy(s).

	
3.3 Users have the right to have written advance notice of this policy
	and resource-specific polices which apply to them before
	requesting access.


3.4 Users have the responsibility to respect the policies established
	by the administrators of networks not controlled or
	administrated by MSUCS while using MSUCS resources.



4.0 Priority Utilization of MSUCS resources.

4.1 Users have the responsibility to put their academic and
	educational uses of MSUCS resources above their personal use
	at all times.

4.2 Users have the responsibility to yield resources to other users
	who have legitimate resource needs before using resources for
	personal use.

4.3 Users have the responsibility to release or yield any MSUCS
	resources which they are are not actively using, regardless of
	demand for the resource.

	
5.0 Privacy responsibilities and rights.

5.1 Users have the responsibility to respect the privacy of other
	users.  Where users are exposed to private data of other
	users, they are expected to keep such information
	confidential.  This includes, but is not limited to:
	printouts, files, e-mail, data and transmissions which a user
	may be exposed to.

	
6.0 Property rights.

6.1 Users have property rights to the content of their data and
	communications, unless otherwise defined by the user's legal
	contract with MSU.

	
7.0 Academic Freedom and Censorship

7.1 Users have the right to examine a broad range of opinions and
	ideas, including the right to locate, use and exchange
	information and ideas located on MSUCS resources and by using
	MSUCS resources to access other information providers.

		might be offensive/against my morals/politically incorrect."
	With this section I hope to establish a semblance of "academic
	freedom" and "free expression".}

7.2 Users have the right to examine and use all information formats,
	including interactive electronic formats.

	
Rights and Responsibilities of MSUCS
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1.0 Privacy and Confidentiality

1.1 MSUCS has the responsibility to respect the privacy of its users.

	Examples of items which are considered private: files, data,
	communications, and e-mail of a user.

1.2 MSUCS has the responsibility to inform a user, before and at the
	time that they receive authorization, if the user will not
	have privacy rights.

	1.3 MSUCS has the responsibility, at all times, to maintain the
	confidentiality of a user's data including, but not limited
	to: files, e-mail, communications, and printouts.

	1.4 MSUCS has the responsibility of keeping private or confidential
	all printouts made on MSUCS printers which are directly
	serviced by MSUCS employees.

	The operators of the printers will keep the contents of the
	printouts private, if possible.  If privacy is not possible,
	the operators of the printers will maintain confidentiality of
	the contents of the printouts.

	
	Some printers may reside in a "public" area, with no
	employees to exclusively service the printer.  In instances
	such as these, MSUCS cannot provide any reasonable expectation
	of privacy or confidentiality.

		The methods used to keep printouts private or confidential may
	vary from printer to printer.



2.0 Security

2.1 With reasonable cause for suspicion, MSUCS has the right to
	monitor and examine any and all aspects of a system,
	including, but not limited to: individual login sessions,
	communications, data, and e-mail; to determine if a user is
	acting in violation of federal law, state law, local law, or
	the policies set forth in this document.

2.2 MSUCS has the responsibility to correct any unauthorized use of
	resources.

2.3 MSUCS has the right to change any resource, resource identifier,
	or userid for security reasons.  MSUCS has the responsibility
	to contact the user(s) involved or affected and give them
	advance notice of the change.  However, in extreme cases the
	users may not receive any advance notice.



3.0 Regular maintenance and performance duties.

3.1 MSUCS has the right to examine relevant files, e-mail, backups,
	printer listings, data, or other resources to gather
	sufficient information to diagnose and correct problems with
	MSUCS resources.

3.2 MSUCS has the right to terminate or alter the usage of resources
	which are idle, consuming excessive resources, or
	objectionably reducing resource response.

	The definition of "excessive", "objectionably", and "idle" are
	resource-specific and vary depending upon resource
	availability and demand upon the resource.

	MSUCS has the responsibility to try to contact the user before
	any change or modification is made, to allow the user to
	correct the situation themselves.  If MSUCS cannot contact the
	user within a reasonable amount of time, then MSUCS will
	attempt to notify the user, after the fact, of what was
	changed or terminated, and the reasons for the change.

	
3.3 MSUCS has the responsibility to provide advance notice of resource
	shutdowns, maintenance, modifications, upgrades, or changes so
	that users may plan around periods of resource unavailability.

	However, in the event of an emergency, MSUCS has the right to
	shut down or modify a resource with little or no advance
	notification.

	
4.0 Policy

4.1 MSUCS has the responsibility to ensure that all users have access
	to this policy and any resource specific policy before and
	during the use of a resource.

	Therefore, MSUCS will make this policy, and any resource
	specific policies, available for reading at the following
	locations:

		1.  The Academic Computer Center.
		2.  In a conspicuous place on the CWIS(s).
		3.  If possible, on the resource being used.

	In addition, MSUCS will make this policy available at a local
